# Security headers, merged by @sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare with the
# autogenerated immutable-asset-caching rules it appends to this file at
# build time (see .svelte-kit/cloudflare/_headers after a build) — don't
# remove this file expecting those rules to survive on their own.
#
# HSTS / X-Frame-Options / COOP are safe to enforce outright: none of them
# depend on what Google Tag Manager ends up injecting at runtime.
#
# The CSP is Report-Only on purpose. GTM's container is managed externally
# (not in this repo) and can inject scripts/beacons this policy doesn't yet
# know about — shipping it as an enforcing policy risks silently breaking
# analytics on a live site. Report-Only lets real violations show up in the
# browser console with nothing actually blocked; once a look at those
# confirms the allowlist below is complete, flip the directive name to
# `Content-Security-Policy` to start enforcing it.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://api.digitaldustlibrary.com; media-src 'self' https://api.digitaldustlibrary.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.digitaldustlibrary.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://www.googletagmanager.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
